  "notes": "Qassim Cement Company (ticker 3040, a Saudi Joint Stock Company) audited consolidated financial statements for the year ended 31 December 2025 with FY2024 comparatives, from the full audited PDF in the 'Annual / 2025' cell of the Saudi Exchange company-profile 'Financial Statements' tab (Resources/fsPdf/426_0_2026-02-25...). Auditor: BDO Dr. Mohamed Al-Amri & Co. (Ahmed Al Jumah, registration 621); unqualified opinion, dated Dammam 23 February 2026. The consolidated financial statements were approved by the Board of Directors on 28 Sha'ban 1447H (corresponding to 16 February 2026) - Note 41. Amounts are presented in full Saudi Riyals (scale 1) except per-share data. The primary statements (printed FS pages 7-10) are scanned images in the filed PDF (transcribed from page renders at 2.7x); the notes are scanned images with an OCR text layer. Consolidated group; there is **NO non-controlling interest** (net profit and equity are not split), so only total_equity is carried. There are no discontinued operations - the standard pre-tax - zakat bridge applies. **FY2024 comparatives are RESTATED (Note 37):** during H1 2025 the Group finalised the IFRS 3 purchase price allocation for Hail Cement Company (acquired 2024), restating the 31 December 2024 comparatives retrospectively (PP&E +SAR 77.3m among other adjustments); the figures carried here are the restated comparatives as presented on the face statements. goodwill is the reported 'Goodwill' line (from the Hail Cement acquisition). long_term_investments combines the non-current 'Financial investments at FVTPL' (SAR 184,873,756k) and 'Financial investments at amortized cost' (SAR 100,000,000k); short_term_investments is the current 'Financial investments at FVTPL'. investment_property_value is 'Investment properties'; additional_paid_in_capital is 'Additional Share capital'; treasury_shares is the negative 'Treasury shares' line; other_reserves combines the 'Statutory reserve' and the 'Other reserve' (EOSB remeasurement); provisions is 'Provision for site restoration' (quarry); defined_benefit_obligation is 'Employees' benefit obligations'; current_debt is 'Short term borrowing' (nil FY2024, so no FY2024 fact is carried); other_current_liabilities combines 'Dividends' payable' and 'Other Provision'; zakat_payable is 'Zakat Provision'; lease_liabilities_noncurrent / lease_liabilities_current are the reported long-term / short-term lease liabilities. On the P&L: impairment_charges is 'Reversal / (allowance) for expected credit loss' (a reversal - positive - in FY2025); other_income is 'Other income, net'; finance_costs is 'Finance costs'; finance_income is 'Income from financial investments at amortized cost'; dividend_income is 'Dividends from investments at fair value through profit or loss'; other_nonoperating_income combines 'Unrealized gains on investments at FVTPL, net' and 'Realized gains on investments at FVTPL'; income_taxes_and_zakat is the 'Zakat' charge. On the cash-flow statement: depreciation_amortization combines PP&E depreciation, intangible-asset amortisation and right-of-use-asset depreciation; capex combines 'Paid to purchase property, plant and equipment' and 'Paid to purchase intangible assets'; zakat_paid is 'Zakat paid'; debt_issued is 'Proceeds from short term borrowings' (FY2025 only); lease_payments is 'Lease payments'; dividends_paid is 'Paid dividends'; the cash-flow statement discloses no separate finance-cost-paid line, so interest_paid is not carried, and it has no FX-on-cash line; its closing balance equals the balance-sheet 'Cash and cash equivalents' line exactly. Statement page references are the printed FS page numbers: financial position 7, profit or loss and OCI 8, changes in equity 9, cash flows 10.",
